            "MSBM10"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            6.97,
            9.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Deﬁnition 2.1. A braid is a collection of n paths fi : I = [0, 1] 7→D2, called",
          "bbox": [
            151.51,
            246.19,
            491.68,
            257.77
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMBX10",
            "CMMI10",
            "CMMI7",
            "CMR10",
            "CMR7",
            "CMSY10"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            6.97,
            9.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "strands, such that:",
          "bbox": [
            151.51,
            258.27,
            232.81,
            268.23
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMR10"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            9.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "(1) fi(0) = pi.",
          "bbox": [
            158.71,
            282.25,
            221.73,
            293.06
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMMI10",
            "CMMI7",
            "CMR10"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            6.97,
            9.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "(2) fi(1) = pτ(i), for some permutation τ in the symmetric group Σn.",
          "bbox": [
            158.71,
            303.6,
            462.74,
            314.71
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMMI10",
            "CMMI7",
            "CMR10",
            "CMR7"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            6.97,
            9.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "(3) For each t ∈I, fi(t)̸ = fj(t) provided that i̸ = j.",
          "bbox": [
            158.71,
            324.82,
            387.03,
            335.75
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMMI10",
            "CMMI7",
            "CMR10",
            "CMSY10"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            6.97,
            9.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Braids are pictured geometrically as a collection of n strands in three di-",
          "bbox": [
            166.46,
            348.93,
            491.68,
            358.89
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMMI10",
            "CMR10"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            9.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "mensional space. One is usually interested in braids only up to isotopies ﬁxing",
          "bbox": [
            151.51,
            360.88,
            491.71,
            370.84
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMR10"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            9.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "the endpoints of each strand. We will abuse the notation and take the word",
          "bbox": [
            151.51,
            372.84,
            491.71,
            382.8
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMR10"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            9.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "braid to mean an isotopy class. Some examples of braids are the following:",
